   "path": "sections.analysis.3.en",
   "before": "Other forms were available. Washington's own letter offered two: a resignation in writing, or an audience. Congress chose the public audience. The author can imagine other arrangements too, and they are not history: the General and the President facing each other and speaking in turn, or Congress simply taking the commission with no speech at all. Each would have returned the authority, perhaps faster, and each would have cost a visible difference in rank and a complete first-person account on the record.",
   "after": "Other forms were available. Washington's own letter offered two: a resignation in writing, or an audience. Congress chose the public audience. The author can imagine other arrangements too, and they are not history: the General and the President facing each other and speaking in turn, or Congress simply taking the commission with no speech at all. Each would have returned the authority, perhaps faster, but the first would have lost the visible difference in rank, the second the complete first-person account on the record.",
   "issues": [
    "V1-V1"
   ]
  }
